      "A": "Research a low-overhead integer trial-division implementation. Parse fragments once and construct candidates arithmetically, preserving the seven-character suffix width. Replace floating-point divisibility with integer remainder; compare odd/6k±1 trial division against a once-generated prime-divisor table through 24514. Use overflow-safe square bounds and correct small-number handling. Retain full Cartesian enumeration and numerical sorting as a straightforward correctness reference. Measure complete program time, including sieve initialization, especially for small P.",
      "B": "Research contract-derived matching and batch pruning. First establish the invariant: the source pairs provide a perfect matching, and exactly P prime edges means every fragment occurrence has exactly one prime partner. Represent surviving columns with bitmasks; reject proven composites using small-prime residue filters, sharing left-offset and suffix residues across candidates. Propagate forced row/column singletons; otherwise use exact primality tests to identify an edge before removing its endpoints. Never assume the input permutations align. Tune the filtering cutoff and measure whether reduced primality work repays bookkeeping overhead. This matching shortcut is valid only under the certified contract, not the unrestricted contest statement.",
      "C": "Research deterministic Miller–Rabin for the certified numeric range. Compare small-prime prefilters followed by bases {2,7,61}, which suffice below 2^32. Use uint64_t multiplication before modular reduction; candidate products fit safely within that type. Handle small values and bases divisible by the candidate correctly. Keep full Cartesian enumeration initially to isolate the primality-kernel effect. Compare prefilter depths using end-to-end measurements; reject probabilistic tests and unproved modular-reduction shortcuts.",
      "G": "Integrate actual correct programs produced by the research trees. Compare their standalone results before testing selected combinations, particularly C's primality kernel with B's pruning and shared arithmetic parsing. Preserve B's matching invariant explicitly; otherwise enumerate every candidate occurrence. Do not assume gains add: measure each integration under the unchanged harness and retain the fastest validated standalone fallback. Check ascending decimal output, final newlines, leading-zero reconstruction, occurrence counts, and integer safety. Use research and confirmation cases only as authorized; change no tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions, and encode no case-specific answers.",
      "analysis": "The only measured implementation is the correct baseline: mean 0.043314365980525814 seconds. There are no measured optimization results or hotspot diagnostics. Floating-point trial division and repeated string conversion are plausible bottlenecks, not established profiles. The certified contract limits work to 900 concatenations, values at most 600971707, and trial divisors at most 24514. Numeric concatenation is left*10^7+right; leading zeros must still determine suffix width. Small workloads favor serial implementations and careful accounting for startup costs. Use the certified contract rather than resolving the contradictory example or assuming broader contest coverage; all valid certified inputs must remain correct."
    },
